* **Cryptography** (`Catalog/Cryptography/CSIFiShAdvanced.lean`): the abstract
  `CryptoGroupAction` framework underlying isogeny-based key exchange.

The connecting object is the **order of the multiplicative group** `(ℤ/nℤ)ˣ`.
Korselt's criterion is exactly the statement that the order of *every* unit of
`ℤ/nℤ` divides `n - 1`. Recast through a `CryptoGroupAction` of `(ℤ/nℤ)ˣ`, this says
that the `(n-1)`-st power of every group element acts as the **identity** on the
whole space — the order-theoretic phenomenon that makes a Fermat primality test fail
for every base.

The `CryptoGroupAction` / `FreeTrans` structures below faithfully mirror those of
`Catalog/Cryptography/CSIFiShAdvanced.lean`; that catalog file does not currently
elaborate (its final section is truncated), so the relevant definitions are
reproduced here to keep the bridge self-contained and verifiable.

